---
// /residents-benefits-package — linked from application-criteria.astro's
// "Resident Benefits Package" section, the For Tenants nav, and every
// active listing in AppFolio and RentEngine.
//
// Built originally from Red Door's PDF flyer (the old PMW page was just a
// linked graphic). Rewritten Nov 13, 2026 for the updated package, per
// Michael's brief (rbp-page-update.md). Sources, so nobody has to guess
// later where a figure came from:
// - Insurance: AssetProtect coverage summary Michael shared, Nov 2026 (the
//   insurer's summary, not checked against the policy itself). Additional
//   living expenses and medical payments were removed because that summary
//   doesn't include them. The summary's landlord coverages (pet damage,
//   mold/bed bug remediation, loss of rent) are left off on purpose: they
//   protect Red Door, not the resident.
// - Pest control: the vendor's onboarding page for Red Door (Nov 2026),
//   not confirmed by Red Door. Don't list specific pests.
// - Credit building (Piñata, "major credit bureaus", no bureau named) and
//   quarterly filter delivery: Michael, Nov 13, 2026.
// - Utilities (Nutiliti): Red Door's resident flyers. No utility fees here;
//   residents get them in a separate email.
// - Group Rate Internet: $65/month decided by Red Door (Michael, Nov 3 and
//   Nov 12); program details from the vendor's materials. It's separate
//   from the $45 package and only for eligible homes. Don't promise "no
//   installation fees": not confirmed for professional installation.
// Don't name the package vendor or use its logo or badge; resident
// materials carry Red Door's branding. The only prices on this page are
// $45/month (package) and $65/month (internet).
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Resident Benefits Package | Red Door Property Management';
const pageDescription =
  "What's included in Red Door's $45/month Resident Benefits Package: renters and liability insurance coverage, credit building, pest control, air filter delivery, and more.";
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription} path="/residents-benefits-package">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-kicker">For Current &amp; Prospective Residents</span>
      <h1>Resident Benefits Package</h1>
      <p class="lead">One flat monthly fee for insurance coverage and everyday conveniences. Here's exactly what's in it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="criteria-content">
      <p>The Resident Benefits Package is required with every Red Door Property Management lease and is billed as a single $45/month line item alongside rent. It bundles renters and liability insurance coverage with a set of services that make renting easier.</p>

      <div class="criteria-callout is-accent">
        <p><strong>$45/month, included in every lease.</strong> The Resident Benefits Package meets your lease's insurance requirement, so you don't need to buy a separate renters insurance policy to move in.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Insurance Coverage</h2>
      <p>Your Resident Benefits Package includes the following coverage:</p>
      <ul class="fee-list">
        <li><span>Personal belongings</span> <strong>$10,000</strong></li>
        <li><span>Liability for damage to the home</span> <strong>$100,000</strong></li>
        <li><span>Deductible</span> <strong>$500 ($1,000 for burglary)</strong></li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Personal belongings</h3>
      <p>Covers your belongings up to $10,000 against fire or lightning, smoke, explosion, water, wind or hail, and burglary. Burglary means forced entry and requires a police report. Theft without forced entry isn't covered.</p>

      <h3>Liability</h3>
      <p>Covers up to $100,000 of damage you're responsible for to the home, caused by fire, smoke, water, explosion, backup or overflow of a sewer, drain or sump, falling objects, or collapse.</p>

      <h3>Deductible</h3>
      <p>Each claim carries a $500 deductible, or $1,000 for burglary. The deductible is taken out of the claim payment.</p>

      <h3>Not covered</h3>
      <p>Natural disasters such as earthquakes and floods, and normal wear and tear.</p>

      <div class="criteria-note">
        <p><strong>A note on insurance:</strong> the Resident Benefits Package waives your lease's insurance requirement. It isn't personal insurance advice, so consult an insurance professional to evaluate your own needs. See the policy for full details and exclusions.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>Everyday Benefits</h2>

      <h3>Utilities made simple</h3>
      <p>In most homes, utilities stay in Red Door's name through our utility billing partner, Nutiliti, so you don't have to transfer accounts when you move in. You'll get a separate email explaining how utility billing works for your home, including any fees.</p>

      <h3>Credit building</h3>
      <p>On-time rent payments are reported automatically to the major credit bureaus through Piñata, helping you build credit. When you enroll, Piñata sends you a welcome email with an invitation to its app.</p>

      <h3>Air filter delivery</h3>
      <p>Air filters for your home are delivered every quarter for you to install.</p>

      <h3>On-demand pest control</h3>
      <p>Up to four pest control treatments a year, each with a 30-day warranty. Request service at <a href="https://pest.residentforms.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pest.residentforms.com</a> and a vendor will contact you to schedule. Covered pests depend on your plan.</p>

      <h3>Red Door conveniences</h3>
      <ul class="fee-list">
        <li><span>24/7 maintenance hotline</span> <strong>Live person, after hours</strong></li>
        <li><span>Mobile app for rent &amp; maintenance</span> <strong>Free</strong></li>
        <li><span>Online payments via ACH</span> <strong>Free</strong></li>
        <li><span>Returned payment fee waiver</span> <strong>$50 value, 1x/year</strong></li>
        <li><span>Real estate commission discount</span> <strong>$500 credit</strong></li>
      </ul>
      <p>If a payment is returned, Red Door will waive the resulting late fee once per year. And when you're ready to buy a home, using a Red Door agent as your buyer's agent gets you a $500 rebate from our commission toward your closing costs.</p>

      <h2>Group Rate Internet</h2>
      <div class="criteria-callout">
        <p><strong>Separate from the Resident Benefits Package, and only for eligible homes.</strong> Each home's listing says whether it's included.</p>
      </div>
      <p>Many Red Door homes include 1-gig internet through a required Group Rate Internet program, for $65/month. It's billed separately from rent and from the Resident Benefits Package.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>No data caps, and equipment is included.</li>
        <li>Install the equipment yourself or have it professionally installed.</li>
        <li>Activate service by calling the internet provider's activation line before move-in. The activation steps come with your lease.</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="criteria-cta reveal">
        <h2>Questions About Your Lease?</h2>
        <p>Review the full application criteria, or get in touch with our team directly.</p>
        <div class="btn-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/application-criteria">Application Criteria</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact">Contact Us</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
